WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.784
The school plan names a 220-kilogram adult on a third floor with symptomatic bradycardia. Treat that as a scenario brief, not as enough information to choose a treatment or assume the patient must be moved immediately.
学校计划指定一名220公斤的成人，位于三楼并出现症状性心动过缓。应把它视为情景简报，而不是足以选择治疗或假设必须立即移动患者的信息。

00:00:14.784 --> 00:00:33.480
Your first task is to recognize immediate threats, obtain an accurate picture of the patient, request the right level of help and communicate uncertainty. Apply the current authorized pathway and instructor direction; this rehearsal supplies no medication dose or independent treatment order.
首要任务是识别即时威胁、准确了解患者状况、请求适当级别的支援并传达不确定性。应遵循现行授权流程和教师指示；本演练不提供药物剂量或独立治疗医嘱。

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:48.576
Say “the patient who weighs 220 kilograms” or use the patient’s preferred language, rather than using weight as the person’s identity. Explain why a measurement or movement is being considered and ask permission where appropriate.
可以说“体重220公斤的患者”或使用患者偏好的称呼，不要用体重定义一个人。应解释考虑测量或移动的原因，并在适当时征求同意。

00:00:48.576 --> 00:01:03.936
Dignity and safety are compatible. Discuss staffing and equipment needs privately and matter-of-factly; do not promise a transfer method until the actual load limits, patient condition, trained personnel and route are confirmed.
尊严与安全并不冲突。应私下、客观地讨论人员和设备需求；在确认实际承载限制、患者情况、受训人员和路线前，不要承诺转运方式。

00:01:03.936 --> 00:01:18.000
A slow pulse on a screen is a finding, not a complete diagnosis. Confirm the signal and compare it with the patient’s presentation, pulse quality, symptoms, mental status and other available measurements.
屏幕上显示的心率偏慢只是一个发现，不是完整诊断。应确认信号质量，并结合患者表现、脉搏质量、症状、意识状态及其他可用测量进行比较。

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:34.608
Use the current PCP pathway and monitor instructions for the assessment and any intervention. If the patient deteriorates or falls outside your authorization, escalate promptly and communicate what changed rather than improvising a medication plan.
评估和任何干预都要遵循现行PCP流程及监护仪说明。如果患者恶化或情况超出你的授权，应及时升级并说明变化，不要自行编造用药方案。

00:01:34.608 --> 00:01:58.632
The school brief names symptomatic bradycardia but does not provide a rhythm strip, blood pressure, drug history or a completed examination. Obtain those findings in the actual station rather than inventing them. Connect rate with stroke volume and perfusion, and describe the evidence that makes the situation urgent instead of assuming that one rate value defines stability.
学校简报指出有症状心动过缓，但没有提供节律条、血压、药物史或完整检查。应在实际站点获取这些发现，不能虚构。将心率连到每搏量和灌注，说明哪些证据使情况紧急，而不是认为某个心率数值决定稳定性。

00:01:58.632 --> 00:02:22.584
Use the CV and A&P routes to explain competing mechanisms, then use current authorized assessment and escalation for the actual presentation. A conduction finding, a medication effect and an ischaemic problem can overlap. Do not manufacture an ECG diagnosis, a pacing indication or a drug order from this short educational brief.
用CV和A&P路径解释竞争机制，再按实际表现采用现行获准评估与升级。传导异常、药物作用和缺血问题可以重叠。不能从这份简短教学简报编出心电诊断、起搏指征或药物医嘱。

00:02:22.584 --> 00:02:47.880
Ask what the patient actually took and when, including OTC and complementary products, rather than copying an old medicine list. A nodal-slowing drug, pressure treatment or sedating exposure may matter, but the case brief does not establish any of them. Treat these as questions and competing explanations until the patient, packaging or another reliable source supplies the facts.
询问患者实际用了什么、何时使用，包括非处方及辅助产品，而不是照抄旧药单。减慢结点药、降压药或镇静暴露可能相关，但案例简报并未证实。可靠患者陈述、包装或其他来源提供事实前，只能把它们作为问题与竞争解释。

00:02:47.880 --> 00:03:12.096
The PHARM routes connect target, intended effect, accumulation, interaction and adverse response. They do not authorize stopping chronic therapy or giving a reversal medicine on suspicion alone. Keep immediate patient support, current service direction and consultation ahead of a speculative interaction story, and communicate the exposure timeline with its uncertainty.
PHARM路径联系靶点、预期作用、蓄积、相互作用及不良反应，但不授权仅凭怀疑停长期药或给逆转药。即时患者支持、现行服务指示和会诊优先于猜测的相互作用故事；交接暴露时间线及其不确定性。

00:03:12.096 --> 00:03:25.560
For blood pressure, use the manufacturer’s cuff range and the actual measured arm circumference; do not assume that the largest available cuff fits. Poor fit or placement can make a number misleading.
测量血压时，应依据制造商规定的袖带范围和实际测得的臂围；不能假设最大号袖带就一定合适。尺寸或位置不当会使读数产生误导。

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:44.592
For oxygen saturation, assess signal quality and whether the measurement makes sense alongside the patient’s presentation. If the usual site is unsuitable, use an alternate site only when the specific probe instructions and service guidance approve it; record the site and any limitation.
测量血氧饱和度时，应评估信号质量，并判断读数是否与患者表现相符。如果常规测量部位不适用，只有在特定探头说明和服务指导允许时才可使用替代部位；应记录部位及其限制。

00:03:44.592 --> 00:04:08.280
For an original variation, suppose a repeated pressure looks better while the patient becomes less responsive. This variation is not an extra fact from the school case. Check whether the measurement methods are comparable, but do not let the improved number overrule the deteriorating patient. Reassess immediate threats and communicate the new concern through the actual pathway.
原创变化：假设复测血压看似好转，但患者反应下降。此变化不是学校案例额外事实。核查测量方法是否可比，但不能让好转数字推翻患者恶化。应复评即时威胁，并按实际路径沟通新增担忧。

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:29.184
FON helps you update the hypothesis when new cues appear, and MSN asks whether the expected outcome actually occurred. State what improved, what worsened, what is still unknown and what you will reassess next. Do not automatically repeat a previous action or declare success because one task was completed.
FON帮助你在新线索出现时更新假设，MSN要求核对预期结果是否真正发生。说清什么改善、什么恶化、什么未知及下一步复评。不能自动重复先前行动，也不能因为完成某任务就宣布成功。

00:04:29.184 --> 00:04:44.760
The school specifically expects you to plan equipment capacity, staffing and the exit route before movement. Include the entire system—device, accessories, attachment points, surface and the route—not just a label on one stretcher.
学校特别要求在移动前规划设备承载能力、人员配置和撤离路线。应考虑完整系统，包括设备、附件、连接点、地面和路线，而不只是担架上的标签。

00:04:44.760 --> 00:05:02.304
A third-floor route adds stairs, turns, door widths, landings and limited ability to stop. If capacity, trained staff or a safe route is uncertain, pause, protect the patient and request the appropriate resources instead of attempting an improvised lift.
三楼路线意味着楼梯、转弯、门宽、平台以及难以停下等问题。如果承载能力、受训人员或安全路线不确定，应暂停、保护患者并请求适当资源，而不是临时尝试搬抬。

00:05:02.304 --> 00:05:27.336
Before committing to the third-floor move, reconcile the patient’s current needs with the route, trained assistance and the complete equipment system. The patient weighs two hundred twenty kilograms, but safe capacity is not established by adding helpers or checking only one device. Explain the plan respectfully, preserve dignity and arrange the resources the actual situation requires.
第三层移动前，应协调患者当前需要、路线、受训协助及完整设备系统。患者二百二十公斤，但加人或只查一个装置不能证明承载安全。应尊重解释计划、保护尊严，并安排实际情境所需资源。

00:05:27.336 --> 00:05:47.904
Use a receiver check-back so the person assigned a task states what they understood, and confirm that understanding before movement. Agree who watches the patient, what change stops the move and how the team will respond. A perfect equipment plan that loses airway access or misses deterioration is not a complete patient plan.
用接收者复述，让任务接收者说出理解，再确认后移动。约定谁观察患者、什么变化叫停及团队如何应对。若丢失气道接近条件或漏掉恶化，即使设备计划完美也不算完整患者计划。

00:05:47.904 --> 00:06:02.280
The saved plan says the second case should be personalized from an individual Appendix G weakness. Because the official form was not in the saved materials, this lesson cannot know or invent the learner’s actual priority.
已保存计划指出第二个案例应根据个人Appendix G弱项定制。由于现有资料中没有官方表格，本课无法得知或编造学习者的实际重点。

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:17.856
Once the instructor or learner has the real priority, turn it into one observable behavior and practise it in a short original case. Change one cue on the next run so the learner must transfer the skill instead of memorizing a script.
教师或学习者取得真实弱项后，应将其转化为一个可观察行为，并在简短原创案例中练习。下一轮只改变一个线索，促使学习者迁移技能，而不是背诵脚本。

00:06:17.856 --> 00:06:42.624
The second school case is based on the learner’s actual gap; no such individual record is available here. Select the relevant reading only after identifying the observed weakness. If the difficulty involves communication, use the PMHN case method: describe the words and behaviour, ask one open question, listen and check meaning without assigning a stigmatizing label.
第二个学校案例基于学习者实际弱项；这里没有该个人记录。先识别观察到的弱项，再选相关阅读。如果困难涉及沟通，使用PMHN案例方法：描述言语行为、一次一个开放问题、倾听并核对含义，不贴污名标签。

00:06:42.624 --> 00:07:05.952
Psychiatric history does not exclude a simultaneous medical cause of altered behaviour or consciousness. Continue indicated assessment and report objective changes alongside the patient’s account. Change one case cue at a time and observe whether the targeted behaviour transfers, rather than calling a generic scenario a personalized remediation plan.
精神病史不能排除行为或意识变化同时有躯体原因。应继续有指征评估，并将客观变化与患者陈述一并报告。一次改变一个案例线索，观察目标行为能否迁移，不把通用情景称为个人补救计划。

00:07:05.952 --> 00:07:22.368
The school plan asks for one or two system scenarios, extensive documentation and a formal handover. Follow the actual station brief; do not add hidden scoring rules or assume that a provincial licensing standard is the school’s standard.
学校计划要求一到两个系统案例、详细记录和正式交接。应遵循实际站点说明，不要添加隐藏评分规则，也不要假设省级执照考试标准就是学校标准。

00:07:22.368 --> 00:07:37.488
In the debrief, separate the observed action from the interpretation. For example: “The repeat value was not stated in the handover” is observable; “I am bad at communication” is a broad judgment that does not identify a drill.
复盘时应区分观察到的行为与解释。例如，“交接中没有报告复测值”是可观察事实；“我不擅长沟通”则是无法直接指导练习的宽泛评价。

00:07:37.488 --> 00:07:50.736
A useful record distinguishes the patient’s report, your direct observation, monitor data and information from another source. Include the timing and response associated with each important action.
有用的记录应区分患者自述、你的直接观察、监护设备数据及其他来源提供的信息。应写明每项重要行动的时间及对应反应。

00:07:50.736 --> 00:08:08.688
Keep the verbal handover concise but complete enough to support continuity: who the patient is, why care is needed, what changed, what was done, what response followed and what remains unresolved. Use the current service format and confirm transfer of responsibility.
口头交接应简洁但足以维持照护连续性：患者是谁、为何需要照护、发生了什么变化、采取了什么措施、之后有何反应，以及哪些问题尚未解决。应使用现行服务格式并确认责任已交接。
